1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:02,210
Closing time…

2
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:04,550
and the last customer has gone.

3
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:08,920
In Eikon, Today's money shows what is left to do,

4
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:10,700
on one screen.

5
00:00:11,476 --> 00:00:13,616
The courier is at the door.

6
00:00:13,936 --> 00:00:17,776
Paid out: tap his name, type the amount, done.

7
00:00:18,822 --> 00:00:20,312
Now, end of day.

8
00:00:20,352 --> 00:00:22,312
It goes in steps.

9
00:00:23,001 --> 00:00:24,851
Type the till's readings…

10
00:00:25,046 --> 00:00:27,351
and the paid outs come in by themselves.

11
00:00:28,759 --> 00:00:31,289
Count the notes, and the coins.

12
00:00:31,975 --> 00:00:33,175
A little short?

13
00:00:33,355 --> 00:00:36,955
It says so in words, and tells you what to check.

14
00:00:39,357 --> 00:00:42,387
Write what you found, and lock the day.

15
00:00:44,154 --> 00:00:46,599
If the main till ever goes down,

16
00:00:46,679 --> 00:00:48,959
the emergency till keeps selling.

17
00:00:49,154 --> 00:00:50,879
Even with no connection.

18
00:00:52,071 --> 00:00:55,701
And credit notes show what each customer holds.

19
00:00:55,976 --> 00:00:57,901
Find her name, tap use,

20
00:00:57,941 --> 00:01:00,861
and what is left stays on her note.

21
00:01:01,879 --> 00:01:03,839
Eikon. Every euro…

22
00:01:03,879 --> 00:01:04,939
accounted for.

